<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<knowl mode="exercise" xmlns="https://spatext.clontz.org" version="0.2">

    <knowl>
        <content>
            <p>
            Demonstrate and explain how to find the {{diff}} derivative of the following function:
            <me>f(x)={{f}} </me>
        </p>

    </content>
    <outtro>
<p><me>f &apos;&apos; (x)= {{dfdx}}</me></p>
    </outtro>
<!-- {{#marginal}} -->
    </knowl>
     <knowl>
            <intro>
                <p>
The weekly demand for a {{widget}} is  <m>p={{price}}</m> where p is the wholesale unit price in dollars and <m>x</m> denotes the quantity demanded. Suppose that the number of items produced is equal to the number of items sold and that
the cost (in dollars) of producing <m>x</m> {{widget}}s is given by the
following function:
<me>C(x)={{cost_function}}.</me>
                </p>
            </intro>

            <knowl>
            <content>
                <p>Find the marginal  Revenue function </p>
            </content>
            <outtro>
                <p>
                    The mariginal revenue is <m>R'(x)={{marginal_revenue}}</m>
                </p>
            </outtro>
            </knowl>

            <knowl>
            <content>
                <p>Find the marginal Cost </p>
            </content>
            <outtro>
                <p>
                    The marginal cost is <m>C'(x)={{marginal_cost}}</m>
                </p>
            </outtro>
            </knowl>

             <knowl>
            <content>
                <p>Find the marginal Profit </p>
            </content>
            <outtro>
                <p>
                     the marginal profit is <m>P'(x)={{marginal_profit}}</m>.
                </p>
            </outtro>
            </knowl>
              <knowl>
            <content>
                <p>Find the marginal elasticity of demand (Hint: <m>E(p)=-\frac{pf'(p)}{f(p)}
                </m>) </p>
            </content>
            <outtro>
                <p>
                     the elasticity of demand is <m>E(p)={{Elasticity}}</m>.
                </p>
            </outtro>
            </knowl>

        </knowl>
 <!-- {{/marginal}} -->
</knowl>